"In Artonan magic, chaos means demons; high-chaos areas breed demon outbreaks."
"Worlds track a chaos index; outbreak forecasts read like weather reports."
"High chaos degrades a world's System, and replacing it while chaos remains does more harm."
"The System bars low-rank Avowed from high-chaos zones, rating each one's susceptibility."
"Susceptibility means risk of demonic incursion and loss of one's assignment."
"Teleports into high-chaos places use an older, magically violent method."
"The violent teleport is too dangerous for average people and easier with good infrastructure."
"An Avowed's presence stabilizes System calls made from a high-chaos world."
